WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:07.500 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  oh how gorgeous look upon the majesty  and the son of Kurama rex  to be a vault hunter means a life of  tough dirty bloody work it's a lot of  exhausting labor for that precious loot  and the vault hunters could do with a  little vacation in the final Borderlands  2 headhunter DLC pack called sir  hammerlock versus the son of Cromer axe  we see our fatigued anti-heroes take a  trip to beautiful wampum Island where  they hope to kick their feet up and  enjoy a fruity cocktail but just as soon  as you start feeling relaxed sir  hammerlock is snatched away by a neon  blue claw and dragged underground it's  time to get back to work not only is the  final piece of the holiday flavored  headhunter packs the biggest of them  it's easily the best it provides a  challenging story boss a hilarious side  mission a gorgeous new area to explore  and plenty of humorous narration as you  play you are joined by the original  vault hunters who pipe in through your  radio offering aid while providing  fantastically funny back and forth  dialogue a bright blue sky envelops the  beautiful paradise of wampum Island  which is home to sandy beaches jungle  flora an underwater dome and a colossal  water wheel the bright and varied  setting is a playground for equally  vibrant enemies like flying barking  insects and crab boyd's that snap at  your shins from under shallow pools of  water the dark recesses of the island  are inhabited by natives whom you battle  in their home village nestled deep  within a shattered dome these warriors  defend themselves with large wooden  shields while throwing spears  distracting you long enough for their  stunted witch doctors to fling spells in  your direction the slashing and biting  final foe is a formidable challenge but  besting him rewards you with a wealth of  loot to collect and chests to unlock  finishing a story mission isn't the end  of your island adventure with the story  boss gone a new enemy appears hungry for  vengeance  the optional quest isn't that strenuous  but as you come face-to-face with  assassins you must  cut down to size you'll be left in  stitches you don't know what to expect  to come out of these encounters so it's  worth taking the time to see each one to  the comical end this final content pack  ties up remaining loose ends in  marvelous fashion ending on a high note  with the future looking bright for the  battle-weary vault hunters perhaps now  they can start on that well-earned break  [Music]

